classes\ that\ reside\ in\ a\ package\ 'controllers'\ should\ declare\ an\ agent-principal\ stance\ on\ every\ mutating\ route,\ because\ a\ mutating\ route\ is\ reachable\ by\ the\ agent\ principal\ unless\ something\ refuses\ it\ at\ the\ request\ layer,\ so\ leaving\ the\ stance\ unstated\ grants\ the\ capability\ by\ accident\ (JCLAW-1253/1266);\ a\ RequestPrincipal.isAgentOriginated\ guard\ and\ @AgentCallable\ are\ the\ two\ ways\ to\ state\ one,\ and\ @ChatHidden\ is\ not\ among\ them=agent-principal-stance
no\ classes\ should\ access\ target\ where\ a\ call\ or\ method\ reference\ that\ starts\ an\ OS\ process,\ because\ spawning\ an\ OS\ process\ is\ an\ unconfined\ authority\ \u2014\ JEP\ 486\ removed\ the\ SecurityManager,\ so\ the\ child\ is\ bounded\ only\ by\ the\ JVM's\ own\ user\ (JCLAW-1152).\ Start\ a\ sidecar\ through\ services.LocalSidecarDaemon,\ which\ already\ holds\ it;\ wrap\ the\ argv\ of\ a\ process\ model\ output\ can\ steer\ with\ tools.HarnessSandbox;\ grant\ a\ new\ holder\ by\ adding\ its\ lines\ below\ to\ archunit_store/shell-process-spawners\ by\ hand=shell-process-spawners
no\ classes\ that\ do\ not\ have\ fully\ qualified\ name\ 'utils.AppClock'\ should\ access\ target\ where\ a\ wall-clock\ read\ (a\ parameterless\ java.time\ now(),\ System.currentTimeMillis(),\ new\ Date(),\ Calendar.getInstance()\ or\ a\ Clock.system*\ factory),\ because\ wall-clock\ reads\ go\ through\ utils.AppClock\ (JCLAW-1150)\ so\ tests\ can\ bind\ a\ fixed\ clock;\ the\ frozen\ entries\ are\ System.currentTimeMillis\ interval\ baselines,\ not\ reads\ of\ the\ calendar=wall-clock-interval-baselines
no\ classes\ that\ reside\ in\ a\ package\ 'tools..'\ should\ access\ target\ where\ a\ call\ or\ method\ reference\ that\ builds\ a\ filesystem\ path\ directly,\ because\ a\ path\ resolved\ from\ a\ tool\ argument\ must\ be\ contained\ by\ WorkspacePathGuard\ (JCLAW-1152)\:\ resolve\ it\ through\ tools.FsPaths.resolveTargetPath,\ which\ reaches\ the\ guard.\ A\ fixed\ path\ no\ tool\ argument\ reaches\ is\ granted\ by\ adding\ its\ lines\ below\ to\ archunit_store/filesystem-tool-paths\ by\ hand=filesystem-tool-paths
